# Image pins for the LLM gateway (G1.6). Repository state: `make llm-gateway-*` sources this file
# last, so a value in the environment cannot swap the image.
#
# LiteLLM proxy, MIT core only (no enterprise feature is configured), pinned by version AND digest
# so the tag cannot be moved under us (the digest below is the one the registry serves for this
# name; a tag alone can be re-pointed).
#
# v1.111.0 is the newest stable release, published 2026-11-25, and the release this deployment needs
# for the native providers it now uses: `opencode_go/<model>` (the owner's OpenCode Go subscription,
# which needs no api_base and refuses a call without a session id) and `openrouter/<model>`. Owner
# decision 2026-11-27: take the latest stable release rather than the oldest that satisfies the
# repository's 14-day soak; digest-pinning plus `make llm-gateway-test` (this image, our rendered
# config, rotation/cooldown/status/cost against fake upstreams) is what keeps the upgrade honest.
#
# Updating it is a pin bump: a new version and digest, then re-run `make llm-gateway-test` and
# `make llm-gateway-up` against the owner's config.
AEGIS_LLM_GATEWAY_IMAGE=ghcr.io/berriai/litellm:v1.111.0@sha256:ce00096d012719d58c52cecfa373f7c6256dd1b0ff08f6fa607e10e9628f1f46
